From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Name AVP 304 as ETSI ES 283 034 does

ETSI ES 283 034 V2.2.0 clause 7.3.5 defines AVP 304 (vendor ETSI) as
QoS-Profile-Description, and table 10 and the Push-Notification-Request
ABNF (clause 7.1.3) name it so.

Renaming an AVP renames its display filter field (diameter.QoS-Profile
becomes diameter.QoS-Profile-Description), so saved filters and profiles
using the old name need updating.
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
index a48da2b..6746511 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@
 			<gavp name="Maximum-Allowed-Bandwidth-DL"/>
 		</grouped>
 	</avp>
-	<avp name="QoS-Profile" code="304" mandatory="may" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="ETSI" may-encrypt="yes">
+	<avp name="QoS-Profile-Description" code="304" mandatory="may" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="ETSI" may-encrypt="yes">
 		<grouped>
 			<gavp name="Application-Class-ID"/>
 			<gavp name="Media-Type"/>
